            <ArticleTitle>Dyskeratosis Congenita with Adenocarcinoma of Stomach.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>391-392</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 32 years old male had dyskeratosis congenita with adenocarcinoma of stomach along with occurrence of carcinoma of stomch in four affected family members. The patient presented with progressive reticulate hyperigmentation of the face, neck, upper trunk and arms, hypopigmented macules, lacrimation and epigastric pain.</AbstractText>
